Epoch AI data
- The analysis reads Epoch AI's "Capabilities & benchmarking" data (benchmark_data.zip),
  Wayback Machine capture 20261113150458 of https://epoch.ai/data/benchmark_data.zip,
  SHA-256 b07bd2eb34cc26469ea832daa2b17e6088f127caa3361c0ee78bac1d05671814. The zip is not
  included in this repository; data/README.md says where to fetch it.
- Epoch AI's data is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Citation: Epoch AI, "Capabilities &
  benchmarking". Published online at epoch.ai. Retrieved from https://epoch.ai/benchmarks.
- results/ and figures/ contain material derived from that data: Epoch's published ECI
  scores with model release dates and organizations (results/public_data/), scores refitted
  with Epoch's eci-public code at commit e04929ab, the refit's per-benchmark difficulty,
  discriminability and noise estimates (results/bayes_refit/edi_scores_refit.csv), and
  statistics and charts computed from them. Changes from the original: scores were refitted,
  models were filtered and dated as described in README.md, and
  results were summarized. Epoch AI has not reviewed or endorsed this work.

Files from external projects
- The zip also bundles benchmark results that Epoch collects from other projects, in files
  named *_external.csv. These files keep their original licenses; Epoch's CC BY 4.0 license
  does not cover them, and benchmark questions and answers belong to their creators. None of
  these files is redistributed here, but the refitted scores and per-benchmark estimates are
  computed from all benchmark files in the zip, including these.
- Some external files in the zip do not name their source.
